  "placement": "Book page 216, topic 8.2.1, the উদাহরণ with চিত্র ৮.০৪ (a candle between two parallel mirrors M₁ and M₂, with its images x′, x″, x‴ … in a row on both sides, d₁ d₂ d₃ d₄).",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "cm",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the উদাহরণ on book page 216, topic 8.2.1, চিত্র ৮.০৪. A lit candle x stands on a table between two parallel silvered-glass mirrors M₂ and M₁. One tap at a time the student builds the book's row: the image x′ in each mirror with d₁ and d₂ before and behind it, then the image of the image x″ with d₃ and x‴ with d₄, each with its ray traced by the law of reflection; dragging the candle moves every image to its exact place. Then the row runs on both ways, and the camera looks into M₁, where the same images stand as a real pair of mirrors shows them, each reflection a little dimmer. Any named image can be tapped to trace its light. Five test questions. Offline, Bangla and English.",
